{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "Survey study specification (study.json), contract version 1",
  "description": "Generated from the rule table of scripts/survey/survey_spec.py by survey_schema.py; do not edit. A description for editors: the validator (survey-validate) is the authority (docs/survey-toolkit.md, section 3). It also makes these checks, which this schema cannot express, and the path rule (1.6): key-duplicate (a key used twice among the outcomes and attributes together); level-duplicate (a level code used twice within an outcome); max-order-scale (rollup max-order without scale ordinal); max-order-order (rollup max-order with a level that has no order); merge-source (a merge whose source is not a declared level code or NA code); cuts-order (cuts not strictly ascending); labels-count (labels not one longer than cuts); strata-key (a strata key that is not a period number from 1 to the number of labels); codes-outcome-missing (a passage or work study with no outcome whose source is codes); counted-tiers-subset (counted_tiers not a subset of tiers); ne-tier-undeclared (not_established_tier not in tiers); ne-tier-counted (not_established_tier counted); present-code-missing (rollup any-present without a present_code); present-code-level (a present_code that is not a level code of the outcome); present-code-unexpected (a present_code on a rollup other than any-present); exclude-key (an exclude_from_rollup key that is not a passage_attributes key); exclude-value (an exclude_from_rollup value that is not one of that key's level codes); mixed-code (a level, NA or missing code equal to the reserved code mixed); any-present-order (rollup any-present on an ordinal outcome with a level that has no order); rollup-types-key (a rollup_types that is not a passage_attributes key); rollup-by-key (a rollup_by entry that is not a passage_attributes key); period-multiple (more than one attribute of kind period); period-bucketer (a period attribute whose bucketer is not of kind period, or the reverse); frame-column-duplicate (two frame columns with the same name (4.7)); match-all (match all on the bucketer of an attribute that is not of kind flags); match-first-flags (match first on the bucketer of a flags attribute); fallback-flags (a fallback on the bucketer of a flags attribute); match-missing-flags (a flags attribute's table bucketer without match (the default is first; contract silent, refused)); outcome-codes-distinct (an outcome's level codes, NA codes and missing value not all different); attribute-missing (an attribute whose missing value is one of its levels or flags); rollup-by-pipe (a | in a level code of a rollup_by level set); exclude-rule-cells (a passage or work study with an exclude rule other than not-on-question); attribution-missing (a passage or work study without unit.attribution); saturation-fields (a saturation stopping rule without rounds_without_new and min_new_share); legacy-unrecorded-status (a legacy-unrecorded stopping rule in a study that is not legacy); reader-missing (evidence.format plugin without evidence.reader); reader-unexpected (evidence.reader when evidence.format is not plugin (contract silent; refused)); file-missing (a referenced input file that does not exist, unless status is draft); not-covered-s0 (a plug-in, bucket table, vocabulary file or stop-words file not covered by gate S0); legacy-exceptions-status (evidence.legacy_exceptions in a study that is not legacy); legacy-exceptions-uncovered (evidence.legacy_exceptions naming a file that no gate covers); post-step-uncovered (a post_steps file that no gate covers); covers-empty (a gate that covers no file); covers-missing (a covers path that does not exist, unless status is draft); covers-not-file (a covers path that is not a regular file (cannot be hashed; contract silent)).",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "enum": [
        "1",
        "0"
      ]
    },
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*$"
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "question": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "status": {
      "enum": [
        "draft",
        "active",
        "legacy"
      ]
    },
    "vantage": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "module": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Plugin"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        },
        "guide": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "a path under rule 1.6: relative to the study's folder, or repo:-rooted"
        },
        "inclusion": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "module"
      ]
    },
    "vocabulary": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "forbidden": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "a path under rule 1.6: relative to the study's folder, or repo:-rooted"
        },
        "exempt_columns": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "forbidden"
      ]
    },
    "corpus": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
